## WHAT FABRIC-INVOKE IS

fabric-invoke is a lightweight orchestration service with:
  - A single POST /invoke REST endpoint
  - An MCP server exposing fabric_invoke, fabric_route, fabric_status tools
  - An embedded sequence registry (SEQ-01 through SEQ-06)
  - Ollama API dispatch to the 13 specialist models
  - AIANA recall (pre-dispatch) and record (post-resolution) hooks

It is NOT a router — that is fabric-router's job.
It is NOT a specialist — those are the 13 Ollama models.
It is the RUNTIME that executes what fabric-router decides.

Deployment target: git-fabric/fabric-ctrl extension (Option C — ship first)
  Add as src/invoke/ module in the existing Hono server.
  Expose /invoke route on fabric-ctrl's existing HTTP server.
  Extend fabric-ctrl's stdio MCP server with fabric_invoke tool.

Production target: git-fabric/fabric-invoke standalone k3s Deployment
  Namespace: fabric-forge
  REST: port 8080, MCP SSE: port 8081

Language: TypeScript (matches fabric-ctrl's existing stack)
Runtime: Node.js / Bun (follows fabric-ctrl convention)

