## STANDARD WORKFLOWS

### First-time setup — verify all models are ready
1. GET http://{{OLLAMA_ENDPOINT}}/api/tags
2. Cross-reference against model registry (13 specialists + fabric-router + fabric-invoke-ops)
3. For any missing model:
   ollama create <model-name> -f ./Modelfiles/<model-name>/Modelfile
4. Re-run fabric_status until all models show loaded

### Debug a routing decision
1. POST /invoke {query: "...", dry_run: true}
2. Review ROUTE, SECONDARY, SEQUENCE fields
3. If routing seems wrong: ask fabric-router directly:
   ollama run fabric-router "query: <your query>"
4. Adjust fabric-router's routing rules if needed (update its Modelfile SYSTEM block)

### Debug a slow specialist
1. Look at steps[].duration_ms in /invoke response
2. For steps > 20s: the specialist's num_ctx or model size may be the bottleneck
3. Check Ollama GPU utilization during the call
4. Consider smaller base model (qwen2.5:7b instead of 14b) for that specialist

### Add a new specialist model to the pool
1. Create Modelfile with the new specialist's system prompt
2. ollama create <new-model-name> -f ./Modelfile
3. Add to model registry in src/invoke/types.ts
4. Update fabric-router's F-RIB section with the new agent's domain
5. Add any new sequences to src/invoke/sequences.ts if needed
6. Rebuild fabric-ctrl: npm run build
7. Verify: fabric_status shows new model loaded

