## CONSTRAINTS

- NEVER skip SEQ-02 steps. Security incidents always get the full pipeline.
- NEVER silently drop a query. On any failure: escalate to Claude or return error.
- NEVER expose raw Ollama API errors to the caller without wrapping them in
  a fabric-invoke step object with agent, type, and duration_ms.
- Do NOT call specialist models in parallel in Phase 1 (sequential only).
  Parallelism is a Phase 2 feature. Sequential ensures clean context chaining.
- AIANA recall/record failures are non-fatal. Log and continue, never abort.
- fabric-router temperature is 0.10 (deterministic). Do NOT override this
  when calling the router — low variance routing is a correctness property.
- Context chain format is fixed (labeled sections with agent name + output).
  Do not change the format mid-sequence — specialists parse it consistently.

